---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../../../consts';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../../utils/schema';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Is the Chinese Inside Burgundy a translation of the English site?',
    answer:
      'No. It is a separate Chinese-language project co-founded with Jasper Morris MW, with its own editorial line.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is 《勃艮第特级园》 available in English or French?',
    answer: 'No. It is published in Chinese only.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What languages do you work in?',
    answer: 'Chinese, French and English.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can English speakers join the Burgundy trips?',
    answer: 'The trips are conducted in Chinese. Get in touch for other arrangements.',
  },
];

const schema = faqPageSchema(faqs);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Who is Ningbo Mei?"
  description="Ningbo Mei is a Burgundy wine expert and author based in Shanghai, author of 《勃艮第特级园》 and co-founder and Editor-in-Chief of the Chinese edition of Inside Burgundy."
  lang="en"
  path="/en/about/"
  extraJsonLd={[schema]}
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Who is Ningbo Mei?</h1>
    <p>
      Ningbo Mei is a Burgundy wine expert and author based in Shanghai. He is the author of
      《勃艮第特级园》 (Edition EIPL), a Chinese-language study of the 33 Burgundy Grands Crus. In 2019
      he co-founded the Chinese edition of <em>Inside Burgundy</em> with Jasper Morris MW, where he
      serves as Editor-in-Chief. He has travelled to Burgundy every year since 2011 and has visited
      more than 500 domaines.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing on Burgundy in Chinese</h2>
    <p>
      Very few people write about Burgundy in Chinese at a professional level, and almost none do it
      from sustained first-hand fieldwork. That gap is the reason this work exists.
    </p>
    <p>
      Trained at ESC Dijon (Master's in Wine &amp; Spirits Management, 2012), I have worked on a single
      region ever since. 《勃艮第特级园》 covers all 33 Burgundy Grands Crus (Climat / climat) and was
      written from annual visits and repeated tastings across more than a decade — not compiled from
      existing sources.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Chinese edition of <em>Inside Burgundy</em>, co-founded with Jasper Morris MW in 2019,
      adapts his framework for readers in China rather than simply translating it.
    </p>

    <h2>What I do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Burgundy field trips</strong> for Chinese collectors — four to five per year, small
        groups, built around domaine visits
      </li>
      <li><strong>Advanced tasting courses</strong> and a members' tasting community in Shanghai</li>
      <li>
        <strong>《我爱勃艮第》(I Love Burgundy)</strong> — a Chinese-language video series on Burgundy
        appellations, climats and producers
      </li>
      <li><strong>La Paulée Shanghai</strong> — held annually since 2019</li>
      <li><strong>China Advisor</strong>, La Liste</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>On the Chinese Burgundy market</h2>
    <p>
      Based on fieldwork since 2011 and visits to more than 500 domaines, the most common misreading
      of Chinese Burgundy buyers — in both the French trade and the English wine press — is that they
      buy by score and by label. What I see is a rapid shift toward <em>climat</em>-level literacy:
      buyers who ask which parcel, which grower, which vintage, and why. The vocabulary arrived
      faster than the English-language coverage of it did.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also think the counterfeit problem in Asia is discussed almost entirely in the wrong terms.
      The useful question is not how to spot a fake bottle, but how provenance is documented and
      where the chain breaks.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Enquiries about trips and courses:
      <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR.email}`}>{AUTHOR.email}</a>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/notes">Articles</a> (in Chinese)</li>
      <li><a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> (in Chinese)</li>
      <li><a href="/trips">Trips</a> (in Chinese)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <dl class="faq">
      {
        faqs.map((item) => (
          <>
            <dt>{item.question}</dt>
            <dd>{item.answer}</dd>
          </>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <hr />
    <p>{AUTHOR.bioEn}</p>
    <p><em>Updated September 2026</em></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
